      "message": "They\u0027re on 32-bit arm userspace with 64-bit kernels.\nIndeed 32-on-aarch64 6.12 tv/wear cf is being spun up now for regression testing.\n\nI merged https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/3486345\n\u0027NetBpfLoad: on 25Q2+ force 64-bit kernel\u0027 a week ago, which causes a boot failure on a 32-bit kernel, and it hasn\u0027t been reverted.\n\nIt did discover we had some (minimal, very throttled) x86 32-bit kernel CF tests, but those were simply turned down.  32-bit x86 kernels have actually been busted since ~2019...  See the comment in //system/netd/server/XfrmController.h:148\n\nSimilarly there\u0027s some java netlink parsing code that also assumes 64-bit kernel struct ABI.",
